From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FPSensor <gkartyt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:41:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/dtc: Declare yylloc as extern in the lexer

gcc 10+ and lld default to -fno-common, so the lexer's tentative
definition of yylloc clashes with the parser's and the dtc host build
fails with a duplicate symbol. Keep a single definition in the parser
(same idea as upstream e33a814e772c, which could drop the line because
newer dtc lexers already get the declaration from the parser header).
---
 scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l             | 2 +-
 scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l b/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l
index 254d5af8..63da4550 100644
--- a/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l
+++ b/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ LINECOMMENT	"//".*\n
 #include "srcpos.h"
 #include "dtc-parser.tab.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
+extern YYLTYPE yylloc;
 
 /* CAUTION: this will stop working if we ever use yyless() or yyunput() */
 #define	YY_USER_ACTION \
diff --git a/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped b/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped
index a6c5fcdf..36ca0628 100644
--- a/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped
+++ b/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped
@@ -637,7 +637,7 @@ char *yytext;
 #include "srcpos.h"
 #include "dtc-parser.tab.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
+extern YYLTYPE yylloc;
 
 /* CAUTION: this will stop working if we ever use yyless() or yyunput() */
 #define	YY_USER_ACTION \
